+  push(Proof([
+    `The proof is the flux-surface gas of the companion page (*The flux-surface gas*, §§2–25 of the OPEN ledger, every section dated before the run it reports and every pricing lemma read by a second seat), and this paragraph is its chain. The polymer representation is classical: expanding each plaquette weight in characters, f = Σ_{j} d_{j}a_{j}χ_{j} with a_{j} = I_{2j+1}(β)/I₁(β), the partition function is a gas of closed sets of plaquettes whose links all carry an even multiplicity, incompatible when they share a link; a closed branch-free surface at spin ½ weighs u^{F}2^{χ} (Osterwalder–Seiler, Drouffe–Zuber). What the page proves beyond that is a pricing of every decoration of such a surface in exact representation theory rather than in supremum norms: the cut identity (S4′), the lone wall at exactly 3a₁ (S7), the acyclic contacts free (S6), and THE LOCAL THEOREM (Theorem L, §24): the weight of any set of spin-1 plaquettes Y attached to a sheet S, divided by (3a₁)^{|Y|} times the sheet's weight, is at most Π_{v} r_{v} over the vertices Y touches, with r_{v}² = 2^{m_{v}−2}·S(C^{½}_{m_{v}} ∪ Γ_{v}) a Haar integral of the vertex's own star — the sheet's cycle of spin-½ edges and Y's spin-1 chords at v. The stars form a FINITE family, the simple subgraphs of K_{2,2,2,2} on the eight directions at a vertex, so the rate γ(s) = 3θ(s)⁴ with θ(s) = max_{k≤s} r2max(k)^{1/2k} is a finite table: r2max(k) is the exact maximum of the star integral over every star of k chords where every row of the enumeration at k has been read by the exact intertwiner engine (k ≤ 12 and the rows below the engine's cap elsewhere), and on the rows not read it is the lesser of two certified bounds — the Frobenius sieve |S| ≤ Π_{l}√R_{l}, R_{l} the dimension of the invariants at link l, and THE REALIGNED OPERATOR-NORM BOUND (Lemma R, §25): contracting the star's link projectors in any order, |S| ≤ ‖P₁‖_{F}Π_{t}‖M_{t}‖_{op}‖P_{n}‖_{F} with M_{t} the projector realigned along the split, and ‖M_{